-- Ordered quest guidance; source 967020b2b8ca645afcaf90d9bbe5a1b64673947d; generated 2026-10-20.
QuestGuidance.Register("en",200,{
[6369]="700033BB\n1\tTalk to Linda Bolger\tLinda Bolger is in Budgeford, on the road furthest down the hill. Milo Bolger told you that his wife, Linda, had been caught outside when the wolves ran through Budgeford. He told you to go speak with her to learn more.\n2\tSearch the Yale-height\tThe Yale-height is a far distance south-east of Budgeford, beyond Stock Road, not far north-east of Woodhall. The hill is marked by three pillars atop its pinnacle. Milo Bolger asked you to speak with his wife, Linda, about the strange encounter she had with the wolves in the middle of Budgeford. Linda did not have much more to reveal, other than to ask you to investigate the Yale-height, where she saw a large and evil-looking wolf digging in the soil on the night the wolves ran through Budgeford.\n3\tBring rune-inscribed collar to Linda Bolger\tLinda Bolger is in Budgeford, on the road furthest down the hill. Linda Bolger sent you to investigate the Yale-height, where she claimed to have seen a great, evil-looking wolf digging in the ground. During your search you discovered a strange, rune-inscribed collar. You should take the collar to Linda and see if it means anything to her.\n",
[6370]="7001CE9D\n1\tUse the wolf-whistle to summon the Wolf-keeper and defeat him\tPack-howler's Hill is to the south of the Haunted Inn in the Dourstocks. You should go to Pack-howler's Hill and attempt to draw out the wolf-tamer who has trained the Darkrage wolves against the Malledhrim.\n2\tSpeak with Prestadír at the Haunted Inn\tPrestadír is at the Haunted Inn in the Dourstocks. You should return to Prestadír with news of your success.\n",
[6371]="7001AF90\n1\tDefeat barghests in the northern Barrow-downs (total: 12)\tBarghests infest the northern Barrow-downs. The howls of the barghests are enough to frighten less hardy souls near to death. The poor folk of Bree trapped between the Barrow-downs and the Old Forest are weakened by their journey and need rest that the howls will not afford. Reginald Sickleweed asked for your assistance in driving the barghests off.\n2\tTalk to Reginald Sickleweed\tReginald Sickleweed is at the encampment between the Old Forest and the Barrow-downs. At the behest of Reginald Sickleweed, you fought and defeated several barghests in an attempt to silence their howls. You should return to him with news of your success.\n",
[6372]="70034D78\n1\tDefeat barghests near the frozen ponds (total: 8)\tBarghests can be found in the northern Writhendowns near Thrymm's Camp. You should defeat barghests in the Writhendowns.\n2\tCompleted\tYou have defeated several of the dangerous wild barghests in the Writhendowns.\n",
[6373]="7005AB00\n1\tDefeat Chieftain Hrungrod in the keep of Thyrstáth\tChieftain Hrungrod can be found in his throne room in Thyrstáth. You should defeat Chieftain Hrungrod.\n2\tCall Hórin and talk to him or speak to him back at Fellgát\tUse the summoning horn to call Hórin to your side. You should talk to Hórin. If Hórin is no longer with you, you can find him at Fellgát.\n",
[6374]="70060D98\n1\tTravel to Hubo Clayhanger's home\tHubo Clayhanger's home can be found in the village of Nobottle. You should travel to Hubo Clayhanger's home to further discuss your adventures over a cup of tea.\n2\tHubo Clayhanger's home can be found in the village of Nobottle. You should peruse some of Hubo Clayhanger's books while he prepares tea.\t\n3\tHave a cup of tea with Hubo Clayhanger\tHubo Clayhanger's home can be found in the village of Nobottle. You should have a cup of tea with Hubo Clayhanger.\n4\tTalk to Hubo Clayhanger about his unfinished book\tHubo Clayhanger's home can be found in the village of Nobottle. You should talk to Hubo Clayhanger about his unfinished book.\n",
[6375]="70060D99\n1\tTalk to Arno Diggle in The Fox and Fiddle\tThe Fox and Fiddle can be found in the village of Nobottle. You should talk to Arno Diggle in The Fox and Fiddle.\n2\tCollect nails (total: 6)\030Collect planks of wood (total: 8)\tNails and planks of wood can be found scattered around the village of Nobottle. You should collect nails and planks of wood for the display case.\n3\tBuild the display case\tThe Fox and Fiddle can be found in the village of Nobottle. You should build the display case in The Fox and Fiddle where Arno Diggle said you could build it.\n4\tSet the relics in the display case\tThe Fox and Fiddle can be found in the village of Nobottle. You set the forgotten relics in the display case.\n5\tTalk to Hubo Clayhanger in The Fox and Fiddle\030Talk to Arno Diggle in The Fox and Fiddle\tBoth Hubo Clayhanger and Arno Diggle can be found in The Fox and Fiddle. You should talk to Hubo Clayhanger and Arno Diggle.\n",
[6376]="70060D9A\n1\tTravel to Bâr Faroth in Yondershire\tBâr Faroth can be found in northern Yondershire. You should travel to Bâr Faroth.\n2\tDig up forgotten relics (total: 6)\030Make etchings of the ruins (total: 4)\tBâr Faroth can be found in northern Yondershire. You should dig up forgotten relics and make etchings of the ruins at Bâr Faroth.\n3\tBring Hubo Clayhanger what you have collected from the ruins\tHubo Clayhanger's home can be found in the village of Nobottle. You should bring Hubo Clayhanger what you have collected from the ruins.\n",
[6377]="7002EF3D\n1\tFind fallen saddlebags in the East Wall (total: 3)\030Fill the water-skin at the waterfall mentioned by Radwulf\030Find the waterfall mentioned by Radwulf, upstream of the Orc corpses\tRadwulf gave you a water-skin to fill at the waterfall south-east of Mansig's encampment. He also wants you to search the ground between the camp and where you found the horses for their fallen saddlebags.\n2\tBring the saddlebags and the filled water-skin to Radwulf\tRadwulf is at the Rohirrim camp in the East Wall. You have found the fallen saddlebags and filled the water-skin given to you by Radwulf and should now return to the Rohirrim horse-master.\n",
[6378]="7000E953\n1\tCollect Moose-meat (total: 6)\tMoose can be found throughout the forest surrounding Kauppa-kohta. Cenlieg has asked you to hunt for some moose-meat to feed his bear-friend, Linden.\n2\tTalk to Cenlieg\030Collect Moose-meat (total: 6)\tCenlieg is at Kauppa-kohta, on the eastern shore of the lake. You should bring the meat you gathered back to Cenlieg.\n",
[6379]="7006A6D1\n1\tFeed Heruin near the southern lift\030Feed Maedal near the training grounds\030Feed Gwath near the southern dock\030Feed Cúron out on the pier\030Feed Tathar near the northern lift\030Feed Meril hiding off the main path\030Feed Dagnir near the northern gate\tRaephion has asked you feed his feline friends around the docks in Lond Cirion with the bucket of fish pieces he provided.\n2\tLet the old fisherman know his friends have been fed\tYou have ensured all of Raephion's companions have been fed, return to him back in the docks in Lond Cirion near the bottom of the northern lift.\n",
[6380]="70037B92\n1\tFill the bowls with food from the pot\tGewis has some meals set aside for the guards in the cooking area. Gewis has asked you to fill bowls with soup for the hungry guards.\n2\tBring a meal to Mula, Sergeant of the Guard\tMula is keeping watch on the eastern side of Brockbridge. Gewis asked you to bring a bowl of soup to Mula, the Sergeant of the Guard.\n3\tThere are guards posted throughout Brockbridge. Gewis asked you to also bring meals to other hungry guards.\t\n4\tTalk to Herefara\tHerefara is keeping watch on the western side of Brockbridge. Gewis suggested that you again speak with Herefara when you are done feeding the guards.\n",
[6381]="7002C2FC\n1\tTalk to Cynred to gain entry to the lock-house\tCynred can be found at the lockhouse in Stangard. You should appeal to Cynred for entry to the lock-house to collect the food stores.\n2\tSearch food-store sacks for rations to give out (total: 4)\tFood-stores can be found in the Stangard lock-house. You should collect food-stores from the sacks in the lock-house.\n3\tHorses can be found in the stables of Stangard. You should bring feed-pouches to the horses so that they will be fed.\t\n4\tBring rations to Tatwine\030Bring rations to Byrnstan\030Bring rations to Wada\030Bring rations to Athulf\tThe Men of Stangard can be found throughout the city. You should bring the men their rations for the day.\n5\tTalk to Gadda near the Mead Hall\tGadda can be found near the Mead Hall in Stangard. You should speak with Gadda.\n",
[6382]="70007FF4\n1\tUse Trap\030Collect Rabbit-carcass\tThere are traps for small game scattered not far to the east and west of Thrasi's lodge. Thrasi asked you to either hunt and kill a live rabbit, or to check his traps and bring back a rabbit carcass for the lynx-mother and her cub.\n2\tTalk to Thrasi\030Collect Rabbit-carcass\tBring the rabbit carcass to Thrasi at Thrasi's Lodge.\n",
[6383]="70035673\n1\tDefeat hungry snow-stalkers\tHungry (and therefore violent) snow-cats can be found in the western hills of the High Knolls. You should fend off the hungry beasts who would like nothing better than to eat you up.\n2\tDefeat hungry snow-stalkers (total: 8)\tHungry (and therefore violent) snow-cats can be found in the western hills of the High Knolls. You should fend off the hungry beasts who would like nothing better than to eat you up.\n3\tCompleted\tYou have fended off many of the hungry snow-cats stalking the western hills of the High Knolls.\n",
[6384]="7004A905\n1\tDefeat engorged Zhavár-hai (total: 5)\tEngorged Zhavár-hai can be found within Kâm Lagúrz, the Brokencleft. You should defeat engorged Zhavár-hai.\n",
[6385]="7004AD09\n1\tDefeat plagued dire-wolf (total: 5)\030Defeat Gámnakur\tGámnakur and his pack can be found in the Mokál Rukh. You should defeat Gámnakur and his pack.\n",
[6386]="7004AD0A\n1\tDefeat Shâkrum the Ripper\tShâkrum the Ripper can be found somewhere within Seregost's courtyards. You should defeat Shâkrum the Ripper.\n",
[6387]="700453E3\n1\tSearch the woods of Taur Drúadan for hoofprints\tWhite Stag prints may be found somewhere in the Drúadan Forest. You should search the forest for White Stag prints.\n2\tSpeak with Lhôs-uksa-Wôt\tLhôs-uksa-Wôt can be found near the White Stag prints. You should speak with Lhôs-uksa-Wôt.\n3\tFollow the White Stag prints\tThe White Stag can be found somewhere in the Drúadan Forest. You should follow the trail of hoofprints to find the White Stag.\n4\tSpeak with Lhôs-uksa-Wôt\tLhôs-uksa-Wôt can be found near the White Stag. You should speak with Lhôs-uksa-Wôt.\n5\tApproach the White Stag\tThe White Stag can be found in the Drúadan Forest. You should approach the White Stag.\n",
[6388]="7000E83E\n1\tDefeat snow-beasts in the Bruinen Source (total: 15)\tSnow-beasts may be found throughout the Bruinen Source regions of the Misty Mountains, north of Rivendell, far to the south and east of the North Downs. Handarod has asked you to defeat snow-beasts in the Bruinen Source regions.\n2\tTalk to Handarod\tHandarod is at Esteldín in the North Downs, far to the west and north of the Misty Mountains. You should return to Handarod and tell him of your snow-beast hunt.\n",
[6389]="7004AD0B\n1\tDefeat plagued ash-claw (total: 5)\030Defeat the dire ash-claw\tThe dire ash-claw and its rabble can be found in the Mokál Rukh. You should defeat the dire ash-claw and any other plagued ash-claws you encounter.\n",
[6390]="7004AD0E\n1\tDefeat plague-ridden nerbyg (total: 5)\030Defeat frenzied norbog\tThe frenzied norbog and other plague-ridden nerbyg can be found deep within the Mokál Rukh, behind Seregost. You should defeat the frenzied norbog and other plague-ridden nerbyg.\n",
[6391]="7004AD0F\n1\tDefeat the Sudden Whelmer\tThe Sudden Whelmer can be found in the Mokál Rukh, somewhere in the Chaydash River. You should find and defeat the Sudden Whelmer.\n",
[6392]="7000A9A3\n1\tExamine Subtle Tracks\tTorcall has hidden an Orc-skull somewhere within West Angmar. You have been challenged to recover an Orc-skull that Torcall says is hidden somewhere in West Angmar. He left by the road north of Aughaire and slew an Orc at some point along his journey; if you follow his trail, you may be able to find it.\n2\tBring Orc-skull to Torcall\tTorcall is in Aughaire, in West Angmar. You have recovered the Orc-skull Torcall asked you to find and should now return it to him as proof of your skill as a hunter.\n",
[6393]="70017D85\n1\tComplete the deed \"Dens of the Beasts\"\030Complete the deed \"The Ruins of Eregion\"\tExplore the Elf ruins and dens of the beasts found in Eregion. Tinúriel told you that for you to learn the quickest route to Echad Dúnann in Eregion, you must explore the land and learn its hidden tracks and paths.\n2\tTalk to Tinúriel at Echad Dúnann\tTinúriel is at Echad Dúnann in Eregion. Now that you have explored Eregion and become familiar with its ruins and the dens of the beasts here, you will be able to understand Tinúriel's instruction on the secret way to Echad Dúnann.\n",
[6394]="700174DC\n1\tTalk to Armbeald in the Redhorn Lodes\tArmbeald is at the Orc-Watch in the north-west region of the Redhorn Lodes of Moria. You should find Armbeald, a renowned hunter who should be able to assist you with further advancement at a high level of skill.\n2\tTalk to Armbeald in the Redhorn Lodes\tArmbeald is at the Orc-Watch in the north-west region of the Redhorn Lodes of Moria. You should find Armbeald, a renowned hunter who should be able to assist you with further advancement at a high level of skill.\n",
[6395]="70000035\n1\tMeet Fenton Marshley for further Hunter training\tFenton Marshley is outside the Hunting Lodge east of the town of Archet and north of Bree, in Bree-land. You have been told to speak with Fenton Marshley, a skilled hunter who may have some words for you.\n2\tTalk to Fenton Marshley\tFenton Marshley is outside the Hunting Lodge east of the town of Archet and north of Bree, in Bree-land. You have been told to speak with Fenton Marshley, a skilled hunter who may have some words for you.\n",
[6396]="7000A9A4\n1\tExamine Subtle Tracks\tHorace Roxhythe hid one of his arrow-heads somewhere in Evendim. He crossed from the island of Tinnudir to the mainland on the stone bridge. You have been challenged to follow Horace's trail and recover the arrow-head he hid somewhere in Evendim to prove you are ready for his teachings.\n2\tBring scratched arrow-head to Horace Roxhythe\tHorace Roxhythe is at the Ranger-camp on the island of Tinnudir. You have found the arrow-head that Horace hid in Evendim and should return it to him so he will recognize your skill as a hunter.\n",
[6397]="7000A9A5\n1\tExamine Subtle Tracks\tMaerchiniath's brooch is somewhere in East Angmar. The Ranger Maerchiniath has agreed to teach you how to find secret paths through East Angmar if you can follow the trail he took when he lost his brooch and bring it back to him.\n2\tBring brooch to Maerchiniath\tMaerchiniath is at the hidden camp of Gath Forthnír, in East Angmar. You have recovered the fallen brooch and should return it now to Maerchiniath.\n",
[6398]="7000A94D\n1\tTalk to Trumswith\tTrumswith is at Ost Guruth, the Ruin-hold in the Lone-lands, far to the east of The Forsaken Inn, just north of the Great East Road. You have been told to speak with Trumswith, one of the Eglain at Ost Guruth, who can train you in the ways of the wild.\n2\tTalk to Hogahild\030Examine Subtle Tracks\tHogahild left Ost Guruth near Unni, the dwarf stable-master there, but is now somewhere in the wilderness of the Lone-lands. Trumswith has challenged you to follow the trail of his sister Hogahild. If you can return to him with the name of the only beast he has hunted and spared, information known to Hogahild, he will teach you secret paths through the Lone-lands to Ost Guruth.\n3\tTalk to Trumswith\tTrumswith is in Ost Guruth, the Ruin-hold in the Lone-lands. You have followed her trail to Hogahild, the sister of Trumswith, and she told you the name of the only beast her brother has hunted and spared: the aurochs known as Trampletusk. You should return now to Trumswith with this information and he will teach you what he knows about the wild paths of the Lone-lands.\n",
[6399]="70000043\n1\tBring Warg-tails to Gadaric Munce\030Collect Warg-tails (total: 10)\tWargs can be found among the ruins of Minas Eriol to the south-east of The Forsaken Inn. Gadaric Munce believes that taking the tails of the Wargs who murdered his people will renew the will of the Eglain and humiliate the Wargs and their goblin-masters.\n",
[6400]="70057848\n1\tRecover teeth from Anduin Hunters in Veithhól\tFrom within their den of Veithhól, Anduin Hunters range forth to strike fear into the hearts of those who make their lives here in Misthallow. Capturing the teeth from the ferocious creatures can perhaps ease the minds of the these folk.\n2\tCollect teeth from Anduin Hunters in Veithhól (total: 10)\tWrest the teeth from Anduin Hunters as they range forth from their den of Veithhól. Defeating these foul creatures and claiming a trophy from them can perhaps ease the minds of those live and adventure within Misthallow.\n3\tCompleted\tCompleted.\n",
})
